---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import WorkCard from '../components/WorkCard.astro';
import { getCollection } from 'astro:content';

const work = (await getCollection('work'))
  .filter((e) => e.data.pillars.includes('gtm'))
  .sort((a, b) => b.data.date.valueOf() - a.data.date.valueOf());
---
<Base
  title="GTM systems — Jai Kharbanda"
  description="Enterprise sales for AI apprenticeships: qualification frameworks, outbound systems audited across 100+ campaigns, and pipeline treated as an engineering problem."
  active="gtm"
>
  <section class="hero">
    <h1>GTM systems</h1>
    <p class="sub">
      I sell employer-funded AI apprenticeships to UK enterprises. A typical week is 6 to 10
      discovery calls, 3 or 4 concurrent enterprise cycles, and a mock presentation before any
      pitch that matters. The rest of this page is how the engine behind that works.
    </p>
  </section>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      Everything gets measured, logged and turned into a framework someone else could run. When a
      channel works once, I write the runbook. When it fails, I write down why and set kill
      criteria before trying again. Signals decide which accounts get attention; the calendar just
      executes.
    </p>
    <p>
      The distinctive part is that the engine itself runs on AI. Claude Code and MCP drive my
      enrichment, campaign builds and CRM hygiene, with approval gates where a human should stay in
      the loop. Campaigns that used to take an afternoon get built in minutes, which means the
      scarce resource goes back to being judgement.
    </p>

    <h2>Things I've built and stand behind</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>A design partner qualification framework that scores actions, never compliments</li>
      <li>An outbound audit across 100+ campaigns that changed our channel strategy</li>
      <li>A re-engagement workflow that turned dead leads into booked calls, now a standing system</li>
      <li>A members' club talk circuit that works as top-of-funnel for enterprise deals</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Case studies</h2>
    <div class="grid3" style="margin-top: 1rem;">
      {work.map((entry) => <WorkCard entry={entry} />)}
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="subscribe">
    <h2>Talking to your team about AI capability?</h2>
    <p>
      If you're weighing up how to make a workforce properly AI capable, I'm happy to compare
      notes. No pitch unless you ask for one.
    </p>
    <a class="btn" href="mailto:jai.kharbanda@gmail.com?subject=AI%20capability%20for%20our%20team">Email me</a>
  </section>
</Base>
